// Nothing was written outside the draft, so cancel is a clear and
// an event. The host only has to drop its open flag.
//
// THE SCRIM AND THE HEADER X BOTH Select() THIS BUTTON. The scrim
// used to raise OnCancel directly, which left the whole draft and
// the dirty flag standing after the dialog closed.

If(
    (!nfIsFullVersion && cmpDetEditWorkflow.RequestKey <> "")
    || !_cmpWfDirty
    || (cmpDetEditWorkflow.RequireResolved && cmpDetEditWorkflow.UnresolvedCount > 0),
    DisplayMode.Disabled,
    DisplayMode.Edit
)
// RESOLUTION IS THE HOST'S POLICY, NOT THIS COMPONENT'S.
// A template assignment ARRIVES unresolved by design, so a
// host seeding a new request from a template starts at
// UnresolvedCount equal to the assignment count and Save
// could never light up however much was edited. That is
// what RequireResolved is for.
//
// _cmpWfDirty is still required in both modes. Save on an
// untouched draft is a no op worth refusing.

cmpDetEditWorkflow.OnSave()
// RAISES THE EVENT AND NOTHING ELSE. The host reads DraftPhases and
// DraftWorkers and does the write, which is the one swap point
// between a collection only build and a flow backed one.
//
// Canvas has minted NO key. ClientId and PhaseClientId are local
// join columns and the receiver must strip them.
//
// The draft is NOT cleared here. A failed save must leave the work
// on screen, so the host calls Reset on this instance once the
// write succeeds.

Min(
    6 * nfSize.Row + lblAwCurrent.Height
    + 5 * Self.LayoutGap + Self.PaddingTop + Self.PaddingBottom,
    // SIX CHILDREN, SO FIVE GAPS. The six rows are mode, current,
    // picker, goal at DOUBLE height, department and options. Hand
    // counted, and the one thing here that rots when a field is added.
    // It fails safe: an undercount only grows the scrollbar that
    // LayoutOverflowY already provides, it never clips.
    App.Height - conAwHeader.Height - conAwFooter.Height - 4 * nfSpace.Xl
)

